{title: How Firm a Foundation}
{artist: "K" in John Rippon's Selection of Hymns}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune FOUNDATION - Funk's Compilation of Genuine Church Music (1832)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1787, tune 1832: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
How [G]firm a foun[C]dation, ye [G]saints of the Lord,
Is laid for your faith in His [D]excellent word!
What [G]more can He [C]say than to [G]you He hath said,
To [C]you who for [G]refuge to [D]Jesus have [G]fled?
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
"Fear [G]not, I am [C]with thee, O [G]be not dismayed,
For I am thy God, I will [D]still give thee aid;
I'll [G]strengthen thee, [C]help thee, and [G]cause thee to stand,
Up[C]held by My [G]righteous, om[D]nipotent [G]hand."
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
"When [G]through fiery [C]trials thy [G]pathway shall lie,
My grace, all sufficient, shall [D]be thy supply;
The [G]flame shall not [C]hurt thee; I [G]only design
Thy [C]dross to con[G]sume and thy [D]gold to re[G]fine."
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
"The [G]soul that on [C]Jesus hath [G]leaned for repose,
I will not, I will not de[D]sert to his foes;
That [G]soul, though all [C]hell should en[G]deavor to shake,
I'll [C]never, no [G]never, no [D]never for[G]sake."
{end_of_verse}
